# Every text file in this repo is LF, in the index and in the working tree, on
# every machine. Without this file that was only true by luck: core.autocrlf on
# a Windows clone rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, Git prints a warning per
# touched file, and a diff can fill with line-ending churn that buries the real
# change. eol=lf pins the working tree too, so the two Windows clones and any
# future one all see identical bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe is the one consumer that genuinely wants CRLF. gradlew.bat is the
# only .bat here; build-apk.ps1 stays LF like everything else, since PowerShell
# does not care.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binaries, named so text=auto can never misjudge one. Git usually detects
# these on its own; being explicit costs nothing and removes "usually".
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.apk binary
*.wasm binary
